# Scoped Trivy exceptions. Every entry must be a specific CVE/misconfig ID with a comment
# explaining why it's accepted and an expiry date to revisit it - never a blanket
# suppression. Every entry below was reached by first finding and fixing everything
# that was a real, same-cost-or-cheaper fix (see the `vpc`/`s3`/`eks`/`rds` Terraform
# modules and the Helm `postgres`/`redpanda` StatefulSets for what was actually fixed,
# not waived, in the same pass as this file).

# AWS-0040 "EKS Clusters should have the public access disabled" and AWS-0041 "EKS
# cluster should not have open CIDR range for public access" -
# infra/terraform/modules/eks/main.tf's endpoint_public_access=true is deliberate: this
# is a dev/reference environment meant to be reached by `kubectl`/CI without a VPN or
# bastion host, which a private-only endpoint would require standing up. Revisit by
# 2027-04-22 (6 months) or before this is ever used as anything other than a reference
# environment.
AWS-0040 exp:2027-04-22
AWS-0041 exp:2027-04-22

# AWS-0104 "A security group rule should not allow unrestricted egress" -
# infra/terraform/modules/eks/main.tf's cluster control-plane security group. The EKS
# control plane needs outbound HTTPS to several AWS service endpoints (ECR, STS, the
# EKS API itself, CloudWatch) whose IP ranges are not fixed; scoping this down correctly
# needs VPC endpoints for each of those services, which is a real hardening step, not a
# one-line fix, and out of scope for this milestone. (The equivalent RDS security group
# finding was fixed outright instead of waived - infra/terraform/modules/rds/main.tf's
# aws_security_group.db now has egress=[], since PostgreSQL has no legitimate reason to
# initiate outbound connections at all.) Revisit by 2027-04-22 (6 months).
AWS-0104 exp:2027-04-22

# KSV-0109 "ConfigMap with secrets" - infra/helm/alphadots/templates/configmap.yaml. A
# false positive: the trigger is the substring "TOKEN" inside the non-secret key
# ALPHADOTS_AGENT_MAX_TOKENS (a per-run LLM token-count limit, see
# docs/cost-guardrails.md), not a credential. Every actual credential
# (ALPHADOTS_API_TOKEN, ALPHADOTS_GROQ_API_KEY, POSTGRES_PASSWORD,
# ALPHADOTS_DATABASE_URL) is already in templates/secret.yaml, a real Secret, not here -
# see that file's own header comment. Revisit if ConfigMap keys are ever renamed.
KSV-0109 exp:2027-04-22

# KSV-0014 "Root file system is not read-only" -
# infra/helm/alphadots/templates/{postgres,redpanda}-statefulset.yaml. Both run with a
# writable root filesystem, unlike every stateless service in templates/deployment.yaml
# (which do set readOnlyRootFilesystem: true). Postgres and Redpanda write to more paths
# than just their PVC-backed data directories (Postgres: a unix-socket directory,
# temporary files; Redpanda: its own internal scratch paths) that have not been
# enumerated and tested against a live cluster - k3d cluster creation is currently
# blocked on this machine by an unrelated network restriction (see
# infra/k3d/cluster-config.yaml). Converting these two to read-only root filesystems
# without verifying every write path first risks silently breaking the container rather
# than hardening it. Revisit once a live cluster is reachable to test against.
KSV-0014 exp:2027-04-22
